course: dictionary
lesson: 14870
title: Readiness: prepared, willing and quick
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Readiness is a noun. It names the state of being ready for something. You can see it when people get prepared before an event: «The class packed their bags in readiness for the school trip.» Here readiness means they had everything prepared before the trip.
explain: Readiness can also mean willingness, being happy to do something. «Her readiness to help made the whole group smile.» She did not have to help, but she was happy and willing to do it. The context tells you which meaning fits.
explain: Readiness can also mean quickness, especially in thinking. «His readiness of wit got him out of trouble» means he thought fast and answered cleverly. Ask yourself: what kind of readiness is it? Prepared, willing, or quick? Then try the meaning in the sentence to check it makes sense.
fact: Readiness is a noun, and it is uncountable: you do not say "a readiness" or "readinesses" in everyday writing.
fact: «In readiness for» means prepared for something, as in «in readiness for the storm».
fact: «A readiness to» means willing to do something, as in «a readiness to help».
fact: «Readiness of wit» means quickness in thinking and answering, so it is often used for clever, fast replies.
fact: «State of readiness» means being fully prepared, like a fire crew waiting for a call.
exercise: «The children packed their bags in readiness for the trip.» What does readiness mean here? | Running very fast | Forgetting something important | Being angry about the trip | *Being prepared and ready for something
exercise: «Her readiness to help made the whole group smile.» What does readiness show? | Sleepiness | A rule about the group | Anger at the group | *Willingness, being happy to do something
exercise: «His readiness of wit got him out of trouble.» What does readiness of wit mean? | *Quickness in thinking and answering | A kind of paper | Slowness in thinking | Loss of memory
test: Which phrase means prepared for something? | Full of readiness | Out of readiness | *In readiness for | Ready at last
test: «The fire crew showed great readiness when the alarm rang.» What does readiness show here? | *Being quick and prepared to act | Being slow and tired | Forgetting the alarm | Sleeping through the alarm
exam: Which sentence uses readiness to mean willingness? | Readiness is a bright red colour | The readiness rang the school bell | The team ran out of readiness before the match | *The team showed a readiness to help the new girl
